1. isalpha()	letters only	'abc'.isalpha() → True
   isdigit()	digits only	'123'.isdigit() → True
   isalnum()	letters or digits	'abc123'.isalnum() → True
   isspace()	whitespace only	' '.isspace() → True
   isupper()	all uppercase	'ABC'.isupper() → True

   isalnum() checks whether a string (or in this case, a single character) is alphanumeric meaning it consists only of letters (alphabetic) and/or digits (numeric).
   isalnum is a contraction of "is alpha-numeric":	letters, digits, whitespace and all uppercase only
  
    e.g: 	' '.isspace() → True; 'ABC'.isupper() → True; ','.isalnum()   # False (punctuation)
